The Charge Requirement: The instrument's electromagnetic fields only move and detect charged particles. If a precursor ion splits into a positive ion and a neutral free radical, only the positively charged fragment appears on the spectrum. The neutral piece is lost, dropping its mass value out of the active data.

Precusor isolation (MS1)
What Happens: By combining these laws, the machine sets its electric voltages so that only particles with one specific mass-to-charge (\(m/z\)) ratio can pass straight through the filters.If your precursor ion is \(m/z\ 201\), the machine adjusts its fields so that \(m/z\ 201\) flies straight through, while all other masses (\(m/z\ 150\), \(m/z\ 300\), etc.) are violently bent off-course and smashed into the walls, destroying them. 

